Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||11:08 AM||||Is there any Clear coat out there that can handle high heat?? Or would i be better to get an eastwood powder coat kit?? I have a gun so spraying isn't a problem.<P>Also when painting cast metal surfaces is there a prep I can get so the paint sticks better. I have a few assorted engine parts I want to clean up. Originally I took them off , sanded them and painted them. The paint flated off in a matter of months.<P><BR>Thanks<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||05-15-2001||11:10 AM||||I believe that eastwood has a high heat clearcoat paint also, I've never used it and don't know how it would stand up.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||11:13 AM||||powder coat is way to go. Clear on engine parts turns brownish with heat. No paint ive used stays on my exhaust manifolds for long.Fiero exhaust manifolds are thinner than most cars and retain mega heat as youve seen.(glowing). Best way to get paint to stick to cast parts is sandblasting it clean first. Sandblasting works great to make paint stick to chrome too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||05-16-2001||12:45 AM||||no clearcoat is going to stand up to the heat of an exhaust system, eastwood does make a high temp exhaust manifold/header paint.  My uncle used it on his 1961 impalas exhaust manifolds 6 years ago and they still look brand new.  My friend Marc bought some for his headers for his pontiac 400, but we havent fired it up yet, so I dont know how it will work, but I have faith in eastwood products.  ||||reg||1
